IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- s 2(1) chapeau ("unless the context otherwise requires"), s 2(2) (the affairs of a corporation), s 2(3) (a change of name),
-- s 2(4) to (6) (substantial shareholding and substantial shareholder).
-- Also the coverage rows for the front matter, s 1 and the headings of ss 3, 4, 4A and 4B (no code: not operative or machinery).
-- Imports prelude, daydate and sfa-core.
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Every defined term of s 2(1) is ONE function, named `s 2(1) "<term>" <the thing> is <the term>`, over the facts a person could state.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--     JUST TRUE   the thing is within the term (a limb of the definition is met and no exclusion applies);
--     JUST FALSE  the TEXT says it is not: a definition that says "means" and no limb is met, or an express exclusion ("but does not include");
--     NOTHING     the text does not say: an "includes" definition (an open list) with no listed limb met.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "..."`; every branch that
--   answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A limb the Act hands to the Authority, the regulations or another Act ("prescribed", "specified", "as defined in the
--   Banking Act 1970") is an INPUT named for the fact ("the Authority has prescribed ..."), never a thing read from memory.
--   The definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires" (the chapeau of s 2(1)): that qualification is
--   `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` in sfa-definitions-rest.l4, not repeated here.

§ `s 2(1) chapeau: unless the context otherwise requires`

-- src:1676 | Interpretation
-- src:1678 | 2.—(1) In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 2(1) chapeau (src:1676-1678)
GIVEN
    `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision you are reading otherwise require a different meaning for the defined word?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` MEANS
    IF `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 2(1) chapeau (the answer under a definition) (src:1676-1676)
GIVEN
    `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision you are reading otherwise require a different meaning for the defined word?
    `the answer under the definition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What is the answer under the definition (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING for not covered)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) the answer under a definition, allowing for the context` MEANS
    IF `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): where the context otherwise requires, the Act gives the word no other meaning, so the definition's answer is not the text's answer
    ELSE `the answer under the definition`

-- src:3529 | (2) Any reference in this Act to the affairs of a corporation, unless
-- src:3530 | the contrary intention appears, is to be construed as including a
-- src:3531 | reference to —
-- src:3533 | (a) the promotion, formation, membership, control, business,
-- src:3534 | trading, transactions and dealings (whether alone or jointly
-- src:3535 | with another person or other persons and including
-- src:3536 | transactions and dealings as agent, bailee or trustee),
-- src:3537 | property (whether held alone or jointly with another person
-- src:3542 | or other persons and including property held as agent,
-- src:3543 | bailee or trustee), liabilities (including liabilities owned
-- src:3544 | jointly with another person or other persons and liabilities
-- src:3545 | as trustee), profits and other income, receipts, losses,
-- src:3546 | outgoings and expenditure of the corporation;
-- src:3548 | (b) in the case of a corporation (not being a trustee
-- src:3549 | corporation) that is a trustee (but without limiting
-- src:3550 | paragraph (a)), matters concerned with the ascertainment
-- src:3551 | of the identity of the persons who are beneficiaries under
-- src:3552 | the trust, their rights under the trust and any payments that
-- src:3553 | they have received, or are entitled to receive, under the
-- src:3554 | terms of the trust;
-- src:3556 | (c) the internal management and proceeding of the
-- src:3557 | corporation;
-- src:3559 | (d) any act or thing done (including any contract made and any
-- src:3560 | transaction entered into) by or on behalf of the corporation,
-- src:3561 | or to or in relation to the corporation or its business or
-- src:3562 | property, at a time when —
-- src:3564 | (i) a receiver, or a receiver and manager, is in possession
-- src:3565 | of, or has control over, property of the corporation;
-- src:3567 | (ii) the corporation is under judicial management;
-- src:3569 | (iii) a compromise or an arrangement referred to in
-- src:3570 | section 210 of the Companies Act 1967 or section 71
-- src:3571 | of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution
-- src:3572 | Act 2018 made between the corporation and another
-- src:3573 | person or other persons is being administered; or
-- src:3575 | (iv) the corporation is being wound up,
-- src:3577 | (d) and without limiting sub‑paragraphs (i) to (iv), any conduct
-- src:3578 | of such a receiver or such a receiver and manager, or such a
-- src:3579 | judicial manager, or any person administering such a
-- src:3580 | compromise or arrangement or of any liquidator or
-- src:3581 | provisional liquidator of the corporation;
-- src:3586 | (e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, units of shares
-- src:3587 | in, units of debentures of, and units in a collective
-- src:3588 | investment scheme issued by the corporation;
-- src:3590 | (f) the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise
-- src:3591 | of, the rights to vote attached to shares in the corporation or
-- src:3592 | to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of,
-- src:3593 | such shares;
-- src:3595 | (g) matters concerned with the ascertainment of the persons
-- src:3596 | who are or have been financially interested in the success
-- src:3597 | or failure, or apparent success or failure, of the corporation
-- src:3598 | or are or have been able to control or materially to
-- src:3599 | influence the policy of the corporation;
-- src:3601 | (h) the circumstances under which a person acquired or
-- src:3602 | disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of,
-- src:3603 | shares in, debentures of, units of shares in, units of
-- src:3604 | debentures of, or units in a collective investment scheme
-- src:3605 | issued by, the corporation;
-- src:3607 | (i) where the corporation has issued units in a collective
-- src:3608 | investment scheme, any matters concerning the financial
-- src:3609 | or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or
-- src:3610 | investment contract to which the units in a collective
-- src:3611 | investment scheme relate; or
-- src:3613 | (j) matters relating to or arising out of the audit of, or working
-- src:3614 | papers or reports of an auditor concerning, any matters
-- src:3615 | referred to in paragraphs (a) to (i).
@ref s 2(2) (src:3529-3615)
GIVEN
    `a contrary intention appears in the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a contrary intention appear in the provision you are reading?
    `the matter is the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions or dealings of the corporation (alone or jointly, and as agent, bailee or trustee), or its property, liabilities, profits and other income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure?
    `the corporation is a trustee, is not a trustee corporation, and the matter is who the beneficiaries are, their rights under the trust, or payments they have received or are entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a trustee (but not a trustee corporation), and is the matter the identity of the beneficiaries, their rights under the trust, or any payments they have received, or are entitled to receive, under the trust?
    `the matter is the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the internal management and proceeding of the corporation?
    `the matter is an act or thing done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to it or its business or property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter an act or thing (including a contract made or a transaction entered into) done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to the corporation or its business or property?
    `at that time a receiver or a receiver and manager is in possession of, or has control over, property of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or thing, is a receiver, or a receiver and manager, in possession of, or in control over, property of the corporation?
    `at that time the corporation is under judicial management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or thing, is the corporation under judicial management?
    `at that time a compromise or arrangement under section 210 of the Companies Act 1967 or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 is being administered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or thing, is a compromise or arrangement referred to in section 210 of the Companies Act 1967 or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, made between the corporation and another person or other persons, being administered?
    `at that time the corporation is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or thing, is the corporation being wound up?
    `the matter is the conduct of such a receiver, receiver and manager, judicial manager, person administering such a compromise or arrangement, liquidator or provisional liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter any conduct of such a receiver or receiver and manager, or such a judicial manager, or any person administering such a compromise or arrangement, or of any liquidator or provisional liquidator of the corporation?
    `the matter is the ownership of shares in, debentures of, units of shares or debentures in, or units in a collective investment scheme issued by, the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the ownership of shares in, debentures of, units of shares in, units of debentures of, or units in a collective investment scheme issued by, the corporation?
    `the matter is the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the votes attached to shares in the corporation, or to dispose of or control the disposal of such shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the rights to vote attached to shares in the corporation, or to dispose of, or to exercise control over the disposal of, such shares?
    `the matter is the ascertainment of the persons who are or have been financially interested in the success or failure of the corporation, or able to control or materially influence its policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the ascertainment of the persons who are or have been financially interested in the success or failure, or apparent success or failure, of the corporation, or who are or have been able to control or materially to influence its policy?
    `the matter is the circumstances in which a person acquired or disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of, shares, debentures, units of shares or debentures, or units in a collective investment scheme issued by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the circumstances under which a person acquired or disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of, shares in, debentures of, units of shares in, units of debentures of, or units in a collective investment scheme issued by, the corporation?
    `the corporation has issued units in a collective investment scheme and the matter concerns the undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which they relate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued units in a collective investment scheme, and is the matter any matter concerning the financial or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which those units relate?
    `the matter relates to or arises out of the audit of, or the working papers or reports of an auditor concerning, a matter in the other limbs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to or arise out of the audit of, or the working papers or reports of an auditor concerning, any matter referred to in the other limbs (a) to (i)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) the matter is within the affairs of a corporation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the contrary intention appears" takes the extended construction away; whether the matter is within the affairs of the corporation in the ordinary sense is then left to the provision (FORK F1 in NOTES.md: the other reading is JUST FALSE, "unless" taken as the text's no)
        IF `the matter is the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation` OR `the corporation is a trustee, is not a trustee corporation, and the matter is who the beneficiaries are, their rights under the trust, or payments they have received or are entitled to` OR `the matter is the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` OR (`the matter is an act or thing done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to it or its business or property` AND (`at that time a receiver or a receiver and manager is in possession of, or has control over, property of the corporation` OR `at that time the corporation is under judicial management` OR `at that time a compromise or arrangement under section 210 of the Companies Act 1967 or section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 is being administered` OR `at that time the corporation is being wound up`)) OR `the matter is the conduct of such a receiver, receiver and manager, judicial manager, person administering such a compromise or arrangement, liquidator or provisional liquidator` OR `the matter is the ownership of shares in, debentures of, units of shares or debentures in, or units in a collective investment scheme issued by, the corporation` OR `the matter is the power of persons to exercise, or to control the exercise of, the votes attached to shares in the corporation, or to dispose of or control the disposal of such shares` OR `the matter is the ascertainment of the persons who are or have been financially interested in the success or failure of the corporation, or able to control or materially influence its policy` OR `the matter is the circumstances in which a person acquired or disposed of, or became entitled to acquire or dispose of, shares, debentures, units of shares or debentures, or units in a collective investment scheme issued by the corporation` OR `the corporation has issued units in a collective investment scheme and the matter concerns the undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which they relate` OR `the matter relates to or arises out of the audit of, or the working papers or reports of an auditor concerning, a matter in the other limbs`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "is to be construed as including a reference to" opens the list and does not close it

-- src:3619 | (3) Where the name of a corporation referred to in this Act is
-- src:3620 | changed pursuant to the Companies Act 1967, the change of name
-- src:3621 | does not affect the identity of that corporation or the application of the
-- src:3622 | relevant provisions of this Act or any other written law to that
-- src:3623 | corporation.
@ref s 2(3) (src:3619-3623)
GIVEN
    `the name of the corporation was changed pursuant to the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the name of the corporation changed pursuant to the Companies Act 1967?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(3) the change of the corporation's name does not affect its identity or the application of the law to it` MEANS
    IF `the name of the corporation was changed pursuant to the Companies Act 1967`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a name "changed pursuant to the Companies Act 1967"; a change made any other way is not covered

-- src:3625 | (4) For the purposes of this Act, a person has a substantial
-- src:3626 | shareholding in a corporation if —
-- src:3628 | (a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting
-- src:3629 | shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation; and
-- src:3634 | (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not
-- src:3635 | less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting
-- src:3636 | shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation.
@ref s 2(4) (src:3625-3636)
GIVEN
    `the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have an interest (as section 4 treats it) in one or more voting shares, excluding treasury shares, in the corporation?
    `the total votes attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in?
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes in total are attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(4) the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` AND (`the total votes attached to the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) the person has an interest in` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (`the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation` TIMES 5)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a substantial shareholding in a corporation if (a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation; and (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in the corporation"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the text introduces the test with "if"; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no. The other reading is NOTHING.

-- src:3640 | (5) For the purposes of this Act, a person has a substantial
-- src:3641 | shareholding in a corporation, being a corporation the share capital
-- src:3642 | of which is divided into 2 or more classes of shares, if —
-- src:3644 | (a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting
-- src:3645 | shares (excluding treasury shares) in one of those classes;
-- src:3646 | and
-- src:3648 | (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not
-- src:3649 | less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting
-- src:3650 | shares (excluding treasury shares) in that class.
@ref s 2(5) (src:3640-3650)
GIVEN
    `the share capital of the corporation is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share capital of the corporation divided into two or more classes of shares?
    `the classes of voting shares, with the votes attached to each` IS A LIST OF `Class of voting shares` @desc For each class of voting shares: the votes attached to the shares the person has an interest in, and the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the class (excluding treasury shares)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(5) the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation whose share capital has 2 or more classes` MEANS
    IF `the share capital of the corporation is divided into 2 or more classes of shares`
    THEN
        IF any (GIVEN c YIELD (c's `the votes attached to the voting shares in the class that the person has an interest in` GREATER THAN 0) AND ((c's `the votes attached to the voting shares in the class that the person has an interest in` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (c's `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the class, excluding treasury shares` TIMES 5))) `the classes of voting shares, with the votes attached to each`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a substantial shareholding in a corporation, being a corporation the share capital of which is divided into 2 or more classes of shares, if (a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in one of those classes; and (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting shares (excluding treasury shares) in that class"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the text introduces the test with "if"; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no. The other reading is NOTHING.
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "being a corporation the share capital of which is divided into 2 or more classes of shares"; for a corporation of one class subsection (4) speaks and this one is silent

-- src:3654 | (6) For the purposes of this Act, a person who has a substantial
-- src:3655 | shareholding in a corporation is a substantial shareholder in that
-- src:3656 | corporation.
@ref s 2(6) (src:3654-3656)
GIVEN
    `the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a substantial shareholding in the corporation under subsection (4) (an interest in voting shares carrying not less than 5% of all the votes)?
    `the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person have a substantial shareholding in the corporation under subsection (5) (an interest in voting shares of one class carrying not less than 5% of that class's votes)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(6) the person is a substantial shareholder in the corporation` MEANS
    IF `the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation under subsection (4)` OR `the person has a substantial shareholding in the corporation under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (6) says only that a person who has a substantial shareholding IS a substantial shareholder; it does not say that a person without one is not
